  "summary": "Ticket EVAL-dev-04 from James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, usual hours 06:00-14:00 Chicago). Reports his warehouse office desktop is not coming on the network; shift starts in about an hour. Checked: account is active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0, password not expired. Triage note said user_blocked true, but the account lookup does not show a block; please verify. Device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro, desktop) shows online: false, last check-in 2026-10-11 00:54 UTC, disk 78% free, no warnings. Offline status means the desktop has no network path. No KB article covers a desktop that is offline on the office network. Not yet confirmed: whether other devices or colleagues in the warehouse office are also down (possible office network or switch issue), and whether the desktop was restarted or its network cable checked. Needs Tier 2 to check the office network/switch and the desktop's network connection before the shift starts.",
  "reason": "Desktop is offline with no KB article covering it and no tool to fix network connectivity; P2 with shift starting within the hour."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked your account and your desktop (BL-DT-0108). The account is active and not locked, but the desktop is showing as offline, so it currently has no network connection. I've passed this to our second-level support team with your shift start time in mind. While you wait, please try a full restart of the desktop, and check that the network cable is firmly plugged in at both ends (or that the Wi-Fi is on, if it uses Wi-Fi). If other people in the warehouse office are also unable to connect, please tell us, since that points to the office network rather than your desktop.",
  "internal_note": "Looked up user 8 (James O'Connor, Operations, usual hours 06:00-14:00 Chicago): account active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0, password last set 2026-09-11. Triage said user_blocked true, which does not match the account lookup; please verify. Device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro desktop, assigned to user) is offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 00:54 UTC, disk 78% free, no warnings. No KB article covers an offline desktop; KB-014 and KB-015 are Wi-Fi/slow-network articles and KB-016 is for remote access, none applicable. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) to check the office network/switch and the desktop's connection. Still unknown: whether other office devices are affected and whether the user has restarted or checked the cable. No actions were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
